-- title:
--   Delta-graph degree splits into ordinary and nontranslation degrees
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a finite abelian group. Write $H=G[2]=\{u:2u=0\}$, $K=G[3]=\{v:3v=0\}$, $h=|H|$, $t=|K|$, $n=|G|$, and $q=|2G|$. For a triple support $S$, let $\mathcal F(S)$ be all three-element supports having the same ordered pair-sum counts, and $\mathcal O(S)=\{S+u:u\in H\}$. An ordinary fibre has size $h$; an exceptional fibre has size $2h$. For any fibre $F$, put $F^\circ=\{S\in F:0\notin S\}$. For every finite support $S$ and $k\in\mathbb N$, the graph of square-equivalent triples at symmetric-difference size $k$ satisfies
--
--   $$\deg_{{\rm square},k}(S)=\deg_{{\rm ord},k}(S)+\deg_{{\rm nt},k}(S).$$
--
--   This describes the finite triple-support square fibres.
-- source:
--   Alexandre Couret, Couret — Additive reconstruction: STROBO-4, singleton collisions and RECOH formal proof artifacts, https://zenodo.org/records/23980513; archive COURET_MATHEMATIQUES_20261105.zip, SHA-256 19a3b59aee930df74cab79c27b29e014843bd17179a26fef1261ed6b5a651ab7; file RECOH/lean/Strobo2TorsDeltaCount.lean, lines 90–114; source file SHA-256 ef09c8cbd39579c9c01a7881f4d218e3fdcbd5e90916131e3bd3e7c80a42eb7e; theorem Couret.STROBO2TORS.squareDeltaGraph_degree

